## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, native Apple **`ChangelogModal`** surface at parity with `web/src/components/feedback/ChangelogModal.tsx`, following the established `modals-dialogs` architecture (mirror of `WidgetCatalogueDialog`).

**12 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/ChangelogModal.*`:
- **Logic** (SwiftUI-free): `Adapter` (types), `Projection` (verbatim `compareVersions` port + selection/grouping), `Catalog` (all 6 releases / 189 change lines, generated from the source for fidelity), `Seams` (P1/S11 telemetry, action seam, P1/S8 source, P1/S10 i18n facade, a11y), `Model` (`@Observable`)
- **Views**: `ChangelogModal.swift`, `States` (header/chips/banners + loading/empty/error), `Rows` (collapsible release entry + grouped sections + tone-styled badge), `Previews`
- **i18n** `strings` + **tests** `ModelTests`/`Tests`

**Parity**: first-visit vs since-last-visit subtitle, collapsible per-release entries (version + Latest/Stable/Beta badge + date, first-two open), changes grouped by Keep-a-Changelog category with colored dots, View-full (opens releases URL) / Got-it (markSeen) footer, `view.opened` telemetry. All 6 prompt states render (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/populated + inline-error).

**Verification — all runnable gates GREEN** (raw output pasted in the log):
- `swiftformat --lint`: 0/11 · `swiftlint --strict`: **0 violations** · `check-placeholders`: COUNT=0/EXIT=0 (positive-control proven)
- Isolated SwiftPM build+test: **41/41 pass** under Swift 6 strict concurrency
- iOS-18 + macOS-15 SDK typecheck of the full view layer + real design system: **0 errors**

**Full-app `xcodebuild` — DEFERRED per `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md`** (ran pinned to slot-16): `IOS_EXIT=65` (KMP framework built+staged, then a *pre-existing* sibling-surface defect in `AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions.swift`), `MAC_EXIT=65` (dev code-signing, pre-compile). **0 errors in any ChangelogModal file**; the tier isn't globbed into `project.yml` yet (acceptance-gate's job), so the full-app build is provably unaffected.

